The device manifests in python/klayout_magic_pcells/data/ hold data that
tools/build_manifest.py reads out of each PDK's Magic device generator code
by running it in Magic: device and parameter names, default values, the
labels, order and callbacks of Magic's parameter dialogs, what each _check
proc does to some probe values, and a summary of what Magic draws for the
defaults. The generator code is not included. It comes from:

  sky130A        sky130A.tcl, installed by open_pdks; written by
                 Tim Edwards. The file states no licence.
  gf180mcuD      gf180mcuD.tcl, installed by open_pdks; written by
                 Tim Edwards. The file states no licence.
  ihp-sg13g2     ihp-sg13g2.tcl and the ihp-sg13g2-*.tcl files it sources,
                 Copyright 2025 IHP PDK Authors, Apache License 2.0.
  ihp-sg13cmos5l ihp-sg13cmos5l.tcl and the ihp-sg13cmos5l-*.tcl files it
                 sources, Copyright 2026 IHP PDK Authors, Apache License 2.0.

Since version 0.6 the same folder also holds four data files per PDK, and
docs/gaps/ holds the gap tables. They are generated or measured from the
installed PDKs and ship under the Apache License, Version 2.0, as the
manifests do; the project lead decided this.

  pdk-<pdk>.json       Made by tools/build_pdk_data.py from the PDK's Magic
                       tech file: Magic's DRC rules with their messages,
                       the layers Magic reads and writes, the implants it
                       grows, and its label and pin layers. It adds the
                       layer names of the PDK's KLayout layer properties
                       file, and the layers that the PDK's KLayout LVS
                       deck reads labels from (layer numbers and line
                       numbers only).
  devices-<pdk>.json   Rules for how Magic reads each device from GDS,
                       written by hand; each rule cites the lines of the
                       Magic tech file's GDS input and output styles that
                       it follows.
  readback-<pdk>.json  Measured with Magic: each device's defaults
                       extracted from Magic's database and again after a
                       GDS write and read.
  gaps-<pdk>.json and  Made by tools/build_gaps.py: rule names, values,
  docs/gaps/           line numbers and switch conditions from the PDK's
                       Magic tech file and KLayout DRC decks, and what both
                       tools reported on the case suite in tests/cases/.
                       A switch condition is the text of the condition
                       around a rule in the deck, cut to 60 characters;
                       the rules' own code is not copied.

